hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"892","Ibn 'Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \Allah curses anyone who misguides a blind person and leads him away from the path.\"""""
"893","Isma'il b. Aban narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Hamid b. Bahram narrated to us, saying: Shahr narrated to us, saying: Ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying: While the Prophet was sitting in his courtyard in Makkah, 'Uthman b. Muz'un passed by him. He approached the Prophet and said, ""May I sit with you?"" The Prophet said, ""Yes, sit down."" So 'Uthman sat down, and the Prophet turned his face towards the sky and said, ""The Messenger of Allah has just come to me, and you are sitting."" 'Uthman said, ""What did he say to you?"" He said, ""God commands justice and good deeds and giving to relatives and forbids shameful and unjust deeds. He warns you that He may punish you if you forget."" 'Uthman said, ""That is when my faith became firm in my heart, and I loved Muhammad."""
"894","Anas reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him\npeace, said, \I will enter the Garden with someone who brings up two daughters\nuntil they come of age"
"895","outrage and cutting off\nrelatives.\""896"""
"896","Shihab ibn Ma'mar al-Awqi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""The noble son of the noble son of the noble son of the noble: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim."""
"897","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \My friends on the Day of Rising will be\nthose with taqwa"
"898","Ibn 'Abbas said, \I do not know anyone who acts by this ayat:'Mankind!\nWe created you from a male and a female"
"899","Ibn 'Abbas said, \What do you reckon to be nobility? Allah has\nmade nobility clear. The noblest of you in the sight of Allah is the one\nwith the greatest taqwa. What do you reckon as lineage? The best of you\nin lineage is the best of you in character.\"""""
"900","'A'isha said, \I heard the Messenger of Allah"
"901","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \The spirits are massed armies. Those of\nthem that knew one another are friendly. Those that did not know one another\ndisagree.\"""""
"902","As we were with our sheep, a wolf attacked and took a sheep from us. The shepherd then sought it, and the wolf turned to him and said, ""Who will take care of it on the Day of Reckoning?"" For it has no shepherd except me. The people said, ""Glory be to Allah!"" And the Messenger of Allah said, ""I believe in that, I, Abu Bakr, and Umar."""
"903","The Prophet was in a funeral procession, and he took something and began to level the earth with it. He said, ""There is not one of you but has a place prepared for him in either Paradise or the Fire. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, shall we not be rewarded for our deeds?' He said, 'Work, for each one is created for what he is created for.' He said, 'As for one who is from the people of good, he will be created for the work of the people of good, and as for one who is from the people of wretchedness, he will be created for the work of the people of wretchedness.' Then he recited: ""And as for one who has been given, has been pious, and has been generous with the good."""
"904","Usayd ibn Abi Usayd reported that his mother said, \I said to Abu\nQatada"
"905","'Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani said, \The Messenger of Allah"
"906","Abu Hurayra said, \A fierce wind blew when the people were on the\nroad to Makka while 'Umar was making hajj. 'Umar asked those around him"
"907","He narrated to us Isma'il, who said: Malik narrated to me, from Salih bin Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah bin Abd Allah bin Utbah bin Mas'ud, from Zayd bin Khalid al-Juhani, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) led us in the morning prayer at Hudaybiyah, on the remains of the night, and when the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished the prayer, he turned to the people and said: Do you know what your Lord has said? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: A believer from among My servants has become a disbeliever, and a disbeliever has become a believer. As for one who said: ""We have been rained upon with the blessings of Allah and His mercy,"" that is a believer from among My servants, a disbeliever in the stars. And as for one who said: ""Such and such,"" that is a disbeliever, a believer in the stars."
"908","'When they saw it as a storm cloud advancing on their valleys...'\n(46:24)\""909"""
"909","Abu Nu'ym al-Fadl narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Isa ibn Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Tiyarah (superstitious omen-taking) is shirk, and it is not from us, but Allah removes it by tawakkul (trust in Him)."""
"910","Abu Hurayra heard the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him\npeace, say, \Bad omens. The best of that is the good omen. They asked"
